R"VG(
# sunlost9.vg (D-05): the last broadcast of a radio people that lost its sun (its last recording, `@cast last`; the beacon loops it under the
# drifter's voice), rules `lb.`; and the lessons of the sun after the old time (sunlost8.vg's genre, topics and way, `les.`).
@apart

genre.lastbroadcast (words=40..135)
  {@cast last}{lb.body}

lb.body
  (age<=industrial) {lb.ind.open} {lb.who} {lb.what} {lb.dark} {lb.where} {lb.ask} {lb.ind.close}
  (age<=industrial) {lb.ind.open} {lb.who} {lb.dark} {lb.what} {lb.gift} {lb.ind.close}
  (age=modern) {lb.mod.open} {lb.who} {lb.what} {lb.dark} {lb.where} {lb.ask} {lb.mod.close}
  (age=modern) {lb.mod.open} {lb.who} {lb.dark} {lb.what} {lb.gift} {lb.mod.close}
  (age=futuristic) {lb.fut.open} {lb.who} {lb.what} {lb.dark} {lb.gift} {lb.fut.close}
  (age=futuristic) {lb.fut.open} {lb.who} {lb.dark} {lb.where} {lb.ask} {lb.fut.close}
  (age=farfuture) {lb.ff.open} {lb.what} {lb.dark} {lb.gift} {lb.ff.close}
  (age=farfuture) {lb.ff.open} {lb.dark} {lb.where} {lb.ask} {lb.ff.close}

lb.ind.open (formula people=2)
  Calling anyone. Calling anyone. This is the wireless room under {city}.
  This is the wireless at {hall.below}, calling on every wavelength we have left.
  This is the last operator at the wireless under {city}. Can anyone hear me?
  Calling any ship, any people, anyone. This is {$home}.
lb.ind.close (formula people=2)
  This is {$home}, closing. The message repeats.
  I will leave the set running on the last batteries. It will say this again, and again.
  Repeating. Calling anyone. Repeating.
lb.mod.open (formula people=2)
  This is an emergency broadcast from {hall.below}. This message repeats.
  This is the {city} service, broadcasting from the deep levels on every frequency still working.
  This is the last voice at the transmitter under {city}.
  To anyone receiving: this is {$home}, on the emergency band.
lb.mod.close (formula people=2)
  This message will repeat until the generators stop.
  End of message. It repeats from the beginning.
  If you hear this, we are already gone. The message repeats.
lb.fut.open (formula people=2)
  Automated message. Source: {hall.below}, {city}. Priority: the last.
  This is the archive of the {people} speaking, for whoever comes.
  Message for whoever comes, repeating on every band the machines can reach.
  Recorded by the last of the {people}, for the machines to send.
lb.fut.close (formula people=2)
  The machines will keep this message going for as long as the heat lasts. It repeats.
  End of message. Repeating.
  The message begins again.
lb.ff.open (formula people=2)
  This is the {people}. We are ending, and we are not afraid.
  To whoever is listening: this is the last voice of the {people}.
  We are the {people}, and this is the last thing we say.
lb.ff.close (formula people=2)
  We leave this here, singing to itself, for as long as there is warmth to sing with. It begins again.
  It begins again.
  Listen again; it is the same, and it will be.

lb.who (people=3)
  We are the {people}, of {city} and of the halls below it[, what is left of us|].
  (has:$me) My name is {$me:name}, and I am the last of the {people}[, as far as I know|].
  We were the {people}[, and we|; we] [lived|grew up] on this world when it [had a sun|was warm], [like yours|as yours is].
  You are hearing the {people}, the last of them, [under {mountain}|below {city}].
  We were the {people}, who kept the {herd} and grew {crop} under a sun of our own.
lb.what (people=3)
  Our sun was [lost|taken from us]: {sunway.what}.
  We watched it [go|happen] for generations: {sunway.what}.
  It was not war and it was not sickness[ that ended us|]: {sunway.what}.
  {sunway.what}[, and after that|; after that] the year [did not end|never closed again].
lb.dark (people=3)
  [For|These] {#darkyears|year} there has been no [sunrise|dawn][, and|;] the sea is [ice|frozen], the air lies on the ground as snow, and the stars are out at [noon|midday].
  We have lived {#darkyears|year} in the dark, [at|by] {warm.ground}, eating {dark.food}.
  [The last sunrise was|The sun last rose] {#darkyears|year} ago[; we have|. We have] [counted|marked] every day since, and kept {kept.light} [burning|going].
  We went down when the sun went, and we [lived|held on] [there|below] {#darkyears|year}, by {warm.ground}.
lb.where (people=2)
  We are below {city}, by {warm.ground}. There is nobody else.
  Everyone else is dead. I am down here, by the last warm [stone|vent].
  The others went to sleep by {warm.ground} one by one, and [did not wake|stayed asleep].
lb.ask (people=2)
  Our records are [down here|in the halls below], every one of them; take them, read them, tell someone we were here.
  Do not come to save us[; come|, but come] to [remember|read] us, [that is enough|and that will be enough].
  If you can [hear|understand] this, you can read the rest[: it is all|, which is all] [down here|in the halls below].
lb.gift (people=2)
  If you have a ship, look for the brightest star [behind us|in our sky]: that was our sun, and our road [is still there round it, empty|still circles it, with nobody on it].
  If you can, [go|fly] to the star we came from, and [tell it we were here|say our name there].
  Everything we knew is [down here|in the halls below][. It is yours now|, and it is yours]; we have [no more use for it|nobody left to read it].

# ---- the lessons of the sun after the old time (`les.topic` and the rest: sunlost8.vg) -------------------------------------------------

# the medieval: the questions of the sun, set down by a teacher; a hall's wall
les.med
  (medium=scroll|medium=codex) {les.med.head}\n{les.topic} {les.topic}\n{les.topic} {les.why}\n{les.med.close}
  (medium=scroll|medium=codex) {les.med.head}\n{les.topic} {les.topic} {les.topic}\n{les.below} {les.med.close}
  (medium=scroll|medium=codex) {les.med.head}\n{les.med.teach} {les.topic}\n{les.topic} {les.why} {les.below}\n{les.med.close}
  (medium!=scroll medium!=codex) {les.med.wall} {les.med.words} {les.med.after}
les.med.head (formula people=3)
  The questions of the sun, for the children of {$home}, set down in the {#year:ord} year of {city}, the {#darkyears:ord} without a dawn.
  For the children born under {mountain}, who never saw it: what the sun was. Set down at {$home} by their teacher.
  A lesson for the children of the halls, copied fair at {$home} for those who come after.
  The teaching of the sun, as the old ones gave it, for the young of {$home}.
  Here is what the sun was, in the old ones' words, for the children of {$home}.
les.med.teach
  Children, [listen|hear me], and keep [this as I keep it|these words as I keep them] on this page, for nobody who saw the sun is left to tell you.
  The old ones who saw the sun are dead; I had it from my [mother|grandmother], who had it from hers. [Here is what they said|This is what they told].
les.med.close (formula people=2)
  Learn these, and teach them to your children, so that the sun is not forgotten.
  Here ends the lesson. {god.keep}.
  Say them over at the fire until you have them by heart.
  These are the questions; the answers are the old ones', not mine.
les.med.wall
  (medium=painted) Painted on the vault of the children's hall in {hall.below}: the sun as the old ones drew it, {colour.holy} on dark blue, with the {herd} and the {crop} under it, and these words.
  (medium=painted) On the wall where the children learnt their letters, a sun painted large in {colour.holy}, and under it these words.
  (medium!=painted) Carved over the door of the children's hall in {hall.below}, under a sun cut deep in the stone.
  (medium!=painted) Cut on a stone set where the children sat, beside a carved sun with its rays.
# the industrial: a primer for the schools under the city
les.ind
  {les.ind.head}\n{les.topic} {les.topic}\n{les.topic} {les.ind.why}\n{les.ind.ex}
  {les.ind.head}\n{les.topic} {les.topic} {les.topic}\n{les.ind.below} {les.ind.ex}
  {les.ind.head}\n{les.topic} {les.ind.why}\n{les.topic} {les.topic} {les.ind.below}\n{les.ind.ex}
les.ind.head (formula people=3)
  Lesson {#n}: what the sun was. For the use of the schools of {$home}.
  A primer of the sun, for the children of the {#darkyears:ord} year of the dark. Lesson {#n}.
  The sun: a primer for the schools under {city}, the {#n:ord} lesson.
  For the schools of {hall.below}: the sun, and what it did.
les.ind.why
  It was lost because {les.way}.
  The sun was not taken from us by any fault of ours: {les.way}.
  [The astronomers|Our observatories] saw it coming [generations|a long time] before the last sunrise: {les.way}.
les.ind.below
  [That is why|This is why] we live below, [where the rock is warm|by the warm rock|in the warm ground], and why the lamps are [never let go out|kept burning day and night|tended like children].
  [That is why|So it is that] the halls are kept at the warmth of the old [summers|springs], and [every child learns|the children learn] to [mend a lamp|tend the boilers|read the gauges].
les.ind.ex (formula people=2)
  Exercises: name three things the sun gave us. Ask an old person what the morning was like.
  Questions for the class: what was a day? What was a shadow? Why is the sea ice?
  Copy out the lesson twice, and learn the last line by heart.
  For tomorrow: draw the sun as the old pictures show it.

# the modern: a class on a disc or a reel, a schoolbook
les.mod
  (medium=disc|medium=reel|medium=drive) {les.mod.voice}\n{les.topic} {les.topic}\n{les.topic} {les.mod.why}\n{les.mod.close}
  (medium=disc|medium=reel|medium=drive) {les.mod.voice}\n{les.topic} {les.mod.why}\n{les.topic} {les.topic}\n{les.mod.close}
  (medium!=disc medium!=reel medium!=drive) {les.mod.text}\n{les.topic} {les.topic} {les.topic}\n{les.mod.why} {les.mod.close}
les.mod.voice (formula people=3)
  Good morning, class. Today's lesson is the sun.
  This is lesson {#n} for the schools of the deep levels: the sun.
  Lesson {#n}, the sun. Recorded at {$home} for every class in the levels.
  Settle down, everyone. Today we talk about the sun, which none of you has ever seen.
les.mod.text (formula people=2)
  Unit {#n}: the sun. For the schools of {hall.below}.
  Science for the young, chapter {#n}: our sun.
  What was the sun? A chapter for the schools of {$home}.
les.mod.why
  It was lost because {les.way}.
  Nobody did this to us: {les.way}.
  [The scientists|Our astronomers] [watched|measured] it [for generations|for a lifetime]: {les.way}.
les.mod.close (formula people=2)
  Next lesson: the deep levels, and how they keep us warm.
  Homework: ask someone very old what a sunset looked like, if you can find someone that old.
  That is all for today. Remember: the sun is still there; it is the brightest star in the sky.

# the futuristic: a lesson the machines keep, for the children of the warm levels
les.fut
  {les.fut.head}\n{les.topic} {les.fut.p}\n{les.topic}\n{les.fut.why} {les.fut.close}
  {les.fut.head}\n{les.fut.p} {les.fut.why}\n{les.topic} {les.topic}\n{les.fut.close}
les.fut.head (formula people=3)
  A lesson for the children of the warm levels, recorded by their teacher in the {#darkyears:ord} year of the dark.
  Lesson record, {$home}: the sun. For the archive and the children.
  For the young of {hall.below}: what the sun was. The machines will keep this lesson.
  Today's lesson, for the archive: the sun, for the ones who were born after it.
les.fut.p
  (once) The light in [the gardens|the green levels|the growing halls] is made to be like the sun's, but the sun was [brighter|stronger|whiter], and it [moved across the sky|went over the sky|rose and set].
  (once) We [still keep the day|keep the old day|keep the hours]: the levels go [light and dark|bright and dim] as [the surface did|it was] under the sun, though [nobody needs them to|no one would notice if they stopped].
  (once) The old recordings of the surface show [a blue sky|a sky full of light], [wind in the {tree}|the {herd} in the fields], [the sea moving|people without suits]; [the machines can show you|ask the archive for them].
  (once) The surface was warm then; people [walked|lived|slept] there [without suits|in the open], under [the sky|the sun], and [nobody thought it strange|it was nothing to them].
les.fut.why
  It was lost because {les.way}.
  [We saw it coming|The machines saw it coming] for [generations|centuries]: {les.way}.
  Nobody could have stopped it; {les.way}.
les.fut.close (formula people=2)
  Tomorrow we will go up to the cold door and look at it: the brightest star, which was ours.
  End of lesson. The machines will answer your questions; ask them anything.
  That is the lesson. Be kind to the old ones; they remember the warmth.

# the far future: the thing that hums, a crystal's lesson
les.ff
  (medium=hum) {les.ff.hum} {les.ff.why}
  (medium!=hum) {les.ff.head} {les.ff.p} {les.topic} {les.ff.why} {les.ff.close}
les.ff.hum
  [What hums here|The thing that hums here|This humming] is a lesson. Held, it grows warm [in the hand|against the skin], as warm as the sun once was [on the skin|at noon], and a voice in it says, [again and again|over and over|softly], [this is what it was like|this was the sun|remember the warmth].
  The thing hums at the pitch the old {people} gave the sun; with the hum [comes|rises] a warmth, and a light that [goes slowly|turns] from red to white and back: a day, [made small|kept small|folded up], for children who never had one.
  [Touched|Held to the ear], it [hums|sings] the old day: the cold [before the dawn|of the night], the [warm|white] noon, the [red|long] evening, then the cold again, in the time a child takes to fall asleep.
les.ff.head (formula)
  This is a lesson, kept for the ones born in the dark.
  For the children of the {people}, who will not see it: the sun.
les.ff.p
  For ten thousand years the sun held us and gave us all we had; then it let us go.
  We keep the day in the halls, light and dark in turn, as the sun kept it, so that you will know what a day was.
  The sun was warm, and it was always there; that is the whole of what the old ones remember, and it was enough.
les.ff.why
  It went because {les.way}; we knew long before, and we [chose to stay|stayed].
  We did not leave when {les.way}; [this world was ours|we belonged here], sun or no sun.
  [Long ago|Ten thousand years ago] {les.way}, and the {people} [went down to the warm|stayed with the world]; that is all.
les.ff.close (formula)
  Ask the hum again; it will teach you again.
  Remember it for us.

# ---- the old time's wall, its end (sunlost8.vg's `les.pre`) --------------------------------------------------------------------------

les.pre.then
  Beside it the same figures crowd round a fire in a hole in the ground, and over them there is [nothing at all|only the dark].
  Beside it the round sign [is made again|comes again], smaller, then smaller, then a dot among the dots of the stars.
  Beside it the {herd} lie down, and a line of figures goes into the ground with a fire carried before them.
les.pre.count
  Along the bottom runs a count of strokes, {#darkyears:words} of them; the years without it, the ship thinks.
  Under it all, a row of small figures sit with their hands held out to the round sign as to a fire.
les.pre.ship
  The ship takes it for a lesson: the sun as it was, [made|shown] for children who had never seen it.
  The ship reads it as a teaching for the young: this was the sun, this was its warmth, this was its light on the {herd}.
  It was made, the ship thinks, so that the ones born in the dark would know what the old ones meant by the sun.
les.pre.hands
  Small hand prints cover the lower figures, many of them, children's, pressed there [again and again|over and over].
  The round sign has been touched so often that the {colour.holy} is worn through to the rock in its middle.
  It has been made again more than once, each time a little larger, as if the old one had grown small in the telling.
)VG"
